      "description": "Search Page Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 24 filter options found Category Academic Affairs (46 items) Administrative / Clerical (7 items) Advancement (1 items) Agriculture / Life Science (1 items) Architecture / Construction / Planning (1 items) Business / Accounting / Finance (3 items) Communications / Public Relations / Marketing (5 items) Design / Graphic Design / Industrial Design (3 items) Executive / Director / Management (4 items) Facilities / Skilled Trades (11 items) Fundraising (2 items) Housekeeping (1 items) Human Resources (3 items) Information Systems / Technology (2 items) Instructional / Teaching Faculty (35 items) Legal / Compliance (1 items) Library (1 items) Medical Professionals (11 items) Other (5 items) Performing Arts / Music / Theatre (3 items) Program/Project Management (1 items) Public Safety (3 items) Student Affairs / Services (11 items) Visual Arts / Studio Arts (3 items) Employment Type Search employment types 5 filter options found Employment Type Adjunct Faculty (37 items) Administrative & Professional Faculty (14 items) Classified Staff (32 items) Hourly Wage/Part-Time (3 items) Teaching & Research Faculty (9 items) City Search cities 3 filter options found City Other (2 items) Radford (80 items) Roanoke (12 items) Division Search 5 filter options found Division Academic Affairs (59 items) Enrollment Mgmt & Strategic Comms (3 items) Finance & Administration (23 items) Student Affairs (7 items) University Advancement (2 items) Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Admissions Counselor Radford, Virginia Other Classified Staff Enrollment Mgmt & Strategic Comms The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Read more Project & Event Manager Radford, Virginia Facilities / Skilled Trades Program/Project Management Classified Staff Finance & Administration Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Read more Equipment Repair Technician Radford, Virginia Facilities / Skilled Trades Classified Staff Finance & Administration Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Read more Procurement Specialist, Procurement & Contracts Radford, Virginia Business / Accounting / Finance Classified Staff Finance & Administration Radford University is seeking a detail-oriented and service-focused Procurement Specialist to join the Procurement and Contracts team. Read more Administrative Assistant Radford, Virginia Administrative / Clerical Classified Staff Academic Affairs Come work for a fun group of colleagues in a creative department!  The Department of Design is looking for an administrative assistant.  Provide administrative support to the Department of Design; supervise student workers; maintain calendar(s) and serve as receptionist; maintain budget records; oversee all administrative functions for the main departmental office, including multiple budgets. eVA, Banner, FLAC, Diversity Travel, Emburse, Kuali, Ad Astra and Cognos experience preferred. Read more Assistant Registrar - Compliance Radford, Virginia Academic Affairs Student Affairs / Services Administrative & Professional Faculty Academic Affairs Join the Radford University Office of the Registrar! Read more Full Time Temporary Faculty, Occupational Therapy Roanoke, Virginia Academic Affairs Medical Professionals Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs The Department of Occupational Therapy at Radford University invites applications for a nine-month, full time temporary faculty position beginning in the Fall of 2026 or Spring of 2027. Read more Adjunct Faculty - Marketing Radford, Virginia Academic Affairs Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Instructional / Teaching Faculty Adjunct Faculty Academic Affairs The Department of Marketing in the Davis College of Business and Economics at Radford University invites applications for Adjunct Faculty Positions in Marketing. The department needs adjuncts to teach various marketing classe(s) each semester viz. Principles of Marketing, Professional Selling, Sales Management, Professionalism in Workplace, Retailing, Advertising, etc. Read more Assistant Professor - Nursing Roanoke, Virginia Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Medical Professionals Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Find your place in the College of Nursing! Read more Police Officer Radford, Virginia Public Safety Classified Staff Finance & Administration Radford University Police Department is seeking full-time Police Officer applicants. Read more HVAC Installation & Repair Technician Radford, Virginia Facilities / Skilled Trades Classified Staff Finance & Administration Join our outstanding HVAC team at Radford University! Read more Emergency Management Specialist Radford, Virginia Public Safety Classified Staff Finance & Administration Radford University is seeking an Emergency Management Specialist to join the Department of Public Safety and support a comprehensive, all-hazards emergency management program. This position plays an active role in strengthening the University’s preparedness, response, recovery, and continuity capabilities across the campus community.\n\nThe Emergency Management Specialist supports the development and maintenance of emergency plans and continuity programs; coordinates training, exercises, and preparedness initiatives; assists with emergency notification and crisis communication; supports Emergency Operations Center activities and incident response; and works collaboratively with departments and external partners to enhance University readiness. The position also contributes to public education and outreach efforts designed to build a culture of preparedness throughout the University.\n\nThe ideal candidate will be a collaborative and motivated emergency management professional who can build relationships, manage multiple projects, communicate effectively with diverse audiences, and translate emergency management principles into practical programs and solutions. This is an opportunity to join a growing emergency management program and take an active role in advancing preparedness and resilience across the Radford University community. Read more Clinical Clearance Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean Roanoke, Virginia Administrative / Clerical Classified Staff Academic Affairs Join our team in Health and Human Services as a Clinical Clearance Coodinator and Assistant to the Dean! Read more Administrative Assistant Roanoke, Virginia Administrative / Clerical Classified Staff Academic Affairs The College of Nursing welcomes applications for the Administrative Assistant position at our Roanoke location from organized, motivated and energized individuals. Read more Housekeeping Supervisor Radford, Virginia Housekeeping Classified Staff Finance & Administration Join our team in Facilities Management! We are seeking Housekeeping Supervisor applicants for our 8am - 5pm (M-F) shift. Read more Associate Director, Student Involvement Radford, Virginia Student Affairs / Services Administrative & Professional Faculty Student Affairs Join Radford University as the Associate Director for Student Involvement and help shape the student experience through leadership development, community engagement, student media advising, and signature campus programs. This exciting leadership opportunity combines staff supervision, student organization support, and campus-wide collaboration to empower students to grow, lead, and create their own journey. Read more Assistant Coach, Women's Flag Football Club (Part-Time) Radford, Virginia Student Affairs / Services Hourly Wage/Part-Time Student Affairs The Assistant Coach for the Radford University Women's Flag Football Club Team will support all aspects of the program's operation with a primary emphasis on offensive development, recruiting, and student-athlete success. The Assistant Coach will work closely with the Head Coach to develop and implement offensive strategies, recruit prospective student-athletes, and contribute to the continued growth and competitive success of the Women's Flag Football program within Elevated Club Sports. Read more Weekend Operations Generalist Radford, Virginia Library Classified Staff Academic Affairs Do you enjoy working with college students and providing excellent customer service? Are you organized, dependable, and attentive to detail? If so, we encourage you to apply for the position of Weekend Operations Generalist at McConnell Library, part of the University Libraries at Radford University. Read more Donor-Funded Scholarship Program Manager Radford, Virginia Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Fundraising Administrative & Professional Faculty University Advancement Join our team! We’re hiring a Donor-Funded Scholarship Program Manager to connect students with scholarship opportunities and strengthen relationships with donors and campus partners. Read more Associate Director, Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact Radford, Virginia Academic Affairs Student Affairs / Services Administrative & Professional Faculty Academic Affairs Make a difference while making a living! The Radford University. Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact seeks a motivated individual to manage large projects aimed at building students' capacities to live lives of meaning and purpose through integration of character and public impact into the curriculum and outreach to community partners. This position is grant-funded through June 2028 and may be extended beyond that time frame. More information about the Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact can be found here: https://www.radford.edu/humanities-behavioral-sciences/highlander-center-for-character-public-impact/index.html Read more Executive Director, Strategic Sourcing Radford, Virginia Business / Accounting / Finance Executive / Director / Management Administrative & Professional Faculty Finance & Administration An exciting opportunity awaits at Radford University. Join us today! Read more Undergraduate Progression and Graduation Coordinator Radford, Virginia Academic Affairs Administrative / Clerical Classified Staff Academic Affairs The College of Nursing Undergraduate Department is seeking a Progression & Graduation Coordinator to perform, coordinate, and provide analysis of BSN student progression and graduation activities and provide analyses for both the Radford and Roanoke locations for the College of Nursing under supervision of the Assistant Dean of Undergraduate Nursing. Read more Campus Service Officer (Part-Time) Radford, Virginia Public Safety Hourly Wage/Part-Time Finance & Administration Join our team! Read more Administrative Assistant Radford, Virginia Administrative / Clerical Classified Staff Academic Affairs Join our team in the Department of Geospatial and Earth Sciences! Read more Assistant Director, Admissions Roanoke, Virginia Other Student Affairs / Services Classified Staff Enrollment Mgmt & Strategic Comms Radford University is seeking a dynamic and driven Assistant Director of Admissions to join our team at the Radford University Carilion campus in Roanoke, Virginia. This position plays a vital role in advancing the University's enrollment goals by managing a designated recruitment territory, cultivating meaningful relationships with prospective students and families, and serving as a key ambassador for Radford University and its academic programs. Read more Director of Corporate & Foundation Relations Radford, Virginia Advancement Fundraising Administrative & Professional Faculty University Advancement Join Radford University to lead corporate and foundation relations and help expand philanthropic support for the University's strategic priorities. Read more Communications and Alumni Coordinator Radford, Virginia Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Design / Graphic Design / Industrial Design Classified Staff Academic Affairs Join our team in the College of Nursing! The College of Nursing is seeking applicants for a new role in the largest and rapidly growing college at Radford University. Read more Instructor, Special Purpose - Nursing Radford, Virginia Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Medical Professionals Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Find your place in the College of Nursing! Read more Executive Director of Career and Talent Development Radford, Virginia Academic Affairs Executive / Director / Management Student Affairs / Services Administrative & Professional Faculty Academic Affairs Radford University seeks a dynamic strategic leader to serve as Executive Director of the Center for Career and Talent Development. This role provides visionary leadership for career services, employer partnerships, and talent development initiatives while cultivating external relationships and guiding a team dedicated to connecting students, alumni, and faculty with meaningful career opportunities. Read more Instructor, Special Purpose - Nursing Roanoke, Virginia Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Medical Professionals Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Find your place in the Radford University College of Nursing, where compassion meets excellence! Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 94 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 › Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the we