    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/procurement-specialist-procurement-contracts-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Procurement Specialist, Procurement & Contracts",
      "description": "Procurement Specialist, Procurement & Contracts - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Procurement Specialist, Procurement & Contracts Radford, Virginia, United States Classified Staff Finance & Administration Add to favorites View favorites Title: Procurement Specialist, Procurement & Contracts Application Review Date: 9/30/2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Responsible for administering the contract database in the Procurement and Contracts Department, managing forms, and serving as the Records Retention Officer. Generates reports as needed and oversees the department's funds handling process. Provides support to Procurement Officers as required. Required Qualifications Experience providing excellent customer service with the capability to identify and resolve problems/issues in a timely manner. Detail-oriented with experience managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced, high-volume environment. Experience providing administrative support. Demonstrated excellent computer skills including proficiency with Microsoft including Excel, Word, Outlook and databases. Excellent verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to relate well with a variety of people. Work independently and in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications: Working within a procurement environment with working knowledge of Virginia's e-Procurement Solution (eVA) or comparable electronic procurement platforms. Acquainted with the Commonwealth of Virginia's Purchasing Manual of Higher Education and its Vendors, along with the relevant Governing Rules. Proficient in utilizing databases, spreadsheets, PowerPoint, navigating websites, and developing forms. Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a cover letter and resume for review. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Classified Staff Normal Work Schedule: M-F 8:00AM - 4:30PM Employee Classification: Procurement Officer I Department: Procurement and Contracts Salary: $45,739 - $54,000 (Commensurate with experience and qualifications) Department Contact Name: Kathryn Dicken Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5090 Department Contact Email: kdicken@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 45bba0a3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Finance & Administration-E&G Finance & Administration-E&G Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Business / Accounting / Finance Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) dffd364a Last Name (required) 342a1440 Email (required) adde057c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) c66d3620 Last Name (required) 464899cc Email (required) 7d612038 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary