    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/assistant-registrar-compliance-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar",
      "description": "Assistant Registrar - Compliance - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Registrar - Compliance Radford, Virginia, United States Administrative & Professional Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Registrar - Compliance Application Review Date: 09/30/2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Reporting to the Associate Registrar, the Assistant Registrar - Compliance serves a critical compliance and technical function within the Office of the Registrar. Acting as the University's official liaison responsible for federal student enrollment and graduation data reporting submissions to the National Student Clearinghouse (NSC) and the National Student Loan Data System (NSLDS). The Assistant Registrar - Compliance is responsible for ensuring university compliance with regulatory enrollment reporting requirements. This includes ensuring the accurate and timely transfer of data, timely error resolution, identifying and resolving data issues, maintaining process documentation, and training staff. The Assistant Registrar - Compliance performs regular processing and monitoring of Ellucian Banner processes to ensure timely and accurate enrollment file submissions. This position leads department internal and external audit preparation. Serves as point of contact with university reporting units and oversees department business intelligence report development. Additionally, this position manages the university FERPA training module and assignment of training refresher cycles. The Assistant Registrar - Compliance plays a critical role in compliance, reporting accuracy, data quality, and error resolution. Required Qualifications A Master’s degree, or bachelors degree with equivalent combination of education and experience. Prior experience working with student records in a higher education setting. Demonstrated ability to manage and safeguard sensitive student data in compliance with FERPA and institutional privacy standards. Proven analytical and technical skills, including hands-on experience with database management, data reconciliation, and business process evaluation. Skilled in interpreting and aligning data requirements across departments and systems. Ability to manage recurring data submission deadlines, compliance reporting, and audit cycles with precision and accountability. Skilled in troubleshooting and resolving SIS data integrity issues to support accurate and compliant reporting. Experience utilizing reporting or business intelligence systems such as Cognos. Strong organizational skills with the ability to create and maintain process documentation. Ability to communicate complex technical concepts effectively to non-technical stakeholders and contribute meaningfully to cross-functional teams. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite. Demonstrated aptitude for quickly mastering new technologies and adapting to changing reporting and compliance requirements in the higher education sector. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with National Student Clearinghouse (NSC) enrollment reporting, including submission workflows and resolution of transmission errors. Experience with NSC MyHub. Prior experience with Ellucian Banner. Knowledge of Banner Population Selection functionality or similar system and tool, including the creation, testing, and execution of population selection rules for operational and reporting purposes. Technical proficiency in SQL, or the ability to learn. Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a cover letter and resume. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Administrative & Professional Faculty Normal Work Schedule: M-F, 8:00am-5:00pm, telework eligible Employee Classification: Professional - Lecturer Department: Registrar, Office of the Salary: $49,098 - $56,925 (Commensurate with experience and qualifications) Department Contact Name: Tyler Wertman Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5469 Department Contact Email: twertman@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1819e087 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Student Affairs / Services Academic Affairs Student Affairs / Services Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 8b39ff0a Last Name (required) 275851fe Email (required) c76a10ba Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) 15bd2e37 Last Name (required) ecafe743 Email (required) c5c1e767 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
