    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/emergency-management-specialist-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Emergency Management Specialist",
      "description": "Emergency Management Specialist - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Emergency Management Specialist Radford, Virginia, United States Classified Staff Finance & Administration Add to favorites View favorites Title: Emergency Management Specialist Application Review Date: September 23, 2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Reporting to the Director of Emergency Management, the Emergency Management Specialist works as part of the Radford University Office of Emergency Management under Department of Public Safety team to develop and maintain emergency management programs for Radford University. Typical duties include supporting emergency plan development, conducting training, emergency exercise development and facilitation, along with program development, outreach functions and operational guidance needed for all phases of the emergency management program. •Ensure Radford University emergency plans and activities are consistent with agency directions by the provision of hands-on assistance to university departments •Interpret the requirements of Radford University and other agency policies and provide related guidance to university stakeholders as it relates to emergency preparedness. •Ability to provide leadership in the area of emergency management preparedness, preparing the Radford University community to respond to emergencies that might significantly affect and impact the University; to include: management of the primary, virtual, and alternate Emergency Operations Center (EOC), including operational leadership during EOC activations; management of effective emergency response and recovery resources such as equipment, technology and tools that must be in a ready state for response activity; development and implementation of policies, procedures, and protocols compliant with University policy, as well as federal, state, and local standards and best practices, including virtual EOC platform procedures that ensure the University’s ability to coordinate quickly and efficiently during an emergency; and administration of designated aspects of the crisis and emergency management plans. •Coordinate and lead the continued growth and administration of the University’s Continuity of Operations Planning (COOP) program, including guiding departments through the development, maintenance, and update of continuity plans •Assist in developing, updating, and maintaining campus wide building emergency action plan (BEAP) program as well as the building emergency coordinator (BEC) program. •Maintain, coordinate, and administer departmental outreach and preparedness education programs for students, faculty, staff, and visitors, including the development and management of publications, presentations, website content, marketing materials, and other educational resources. •Assist in planning, developing, coordinating and executing tabletop, functional, and full-scale exercises to enhance familiarity with emergency management. •Ensure consistent delivery of emergency management program efforts at all Radford University locations, through technical support, guidance, and provision of expert assistance to staff on main campus and satellite locations. •Assist with preparing after-action reports and improvement plans. •Assist with the activation and dissemination of emergency notifications and other critical communications for actual or potential incidents affecting the university community. •Attend local and regional workshops, exercises and emergency management events. •Collaborate with internal departments, external agencies, and community partners to coordinate emergency planning efforts, share resources, and foster mutual aid agreements. •Perform other related functions in support of Radford University Department of Public Safety and the Office of Emergency Management program. Required Qualifications • Considerable knowledge of the role of the state, local and federal governments in emergencies; emergency response programs, policies and procedures; and federal and state program regulations. • Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively in a dynamic and diverse environment. • Dependable work ethics with the ability to fit into a team environment characterized by shared accountabilities. • Extensive use of computers to retrieve and input information. • Project planning and development experience. • Experience in policy and best practices pertaining to emergency communications. • Requires the ability to analyze all type emergency situations to determine course of action and solve problems; excellent judgment and decision-making skills. • Certified Emergency Manager certification or ability to obtain within 3 years from the date of hire. • Required: IS-100, IS-200, IS-700, and IS-800. • Required: Certified Emergency Manager (CEM) license or ability to obtain within 3 years from the date of hire. (A bachelor's degree in a related field is required for certification). • Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: • Experience in creating, implementing, and coordinating emergency management planning programs for a large, diverse organization. • Experience in grant writing and management. • Demonstrated customer service experience. • Experience in creating visual presentations, instructional design and the development of training materials. • Expert knowledge of standard communication procedures and equipment; principles and practices of emergency dispatching. • Proven ability to manage stressful situations and changing priorities effectively. • Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. • Preferred experience in using virtual emergency operations center platforms or systems. • Preferred IS-300, IS-400. • Preferred professional certifications: Virginia Professional Emergency Manager (VPEM), Certified Business Continuity Professional (CBCP), Project Management Professional, and/or Master Exercise Practitioner (MEP). Employment Conditions: Valid driver's license; position is designated as essential/emergency personnel Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Classified Staff Normal Work Schedule: 8am-5pm, M-F, Weekend and Evening Hours as Needed, Travel Required Employee Classification: Emergency Coordinator II Department: Emergency Management Salary: $63,000 - $73,000 (Commensurate with education and experience.) Department Contact Name: Peter McCann Department Contact Phone: 540-831-6696 Department Contact Email: pmccann@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert dab62866 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Finance & Administration-E&G Finance & Administration-E&G Categories Public Safety Public Safety Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 80eca596 Last Name (required) 4960b620 Email (required) 5a8bb8a5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) a50ea0d2 Last Name (required) bfe2eb53 Email (required) 5b9969c4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate 