    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/clinical-clearance-coordinator-and-assistant-to-the-dean-roanoke-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Clearance Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean",
      "description": "Clinical Clearance Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean - Roanoke, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Clinical Clearance Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean Roanoke, Virginia, United States Classified Staff Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Clinical Clearance Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean Application Review Date: 9/10/26 Campus Location: Roanoke Job Description Efficiently provides administrative support for clinical agency compliance including but not limited to criminal background checks, CPR certifications, and inoculations records; provides timely response to frequent student phone calls and/or emails. Engages with clinical coordinators within each of the disciplines in the WCHHS regarding clinical clearance requirements for clinical contract agencies. Works with clinical departments within the WCHHS for clinical clearance. Assists the college with winter and spring college commencement ceremonies. Assists with special projects in Waldron College, such as Faculty Research Awards and Waldron College Outstanding Faculty and Staff Awards. Represents the Dean or Associate Dean at meetings when neither are available. Assists with student scholarship awards for College-based scholarships Assist with WCHHS Communication Plan (social media, newsletter, etc.) Assist with and coordinates review efforts of student scholarship awards for college-based scholarships Reviews, and combines updates, for the Waldron College section of the University Catalog; Assists with recruiting and training students in the Waldron Student Ambassadors' program; Prepares reports for the Dean, and department/school chairs and directors, such as enrollment data, data analysis for accreditation support; Assists with and coordinates efforts for Interprofessional Education and Practice (IPE) events and activities in the college; Assists with Governor's School as needed. Assists with Quest, Open House (Highlander Days) and other recruitment related activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Dean to support the college. Required Qualifications Demonstrated positive customer service attitude. Working knowledge of general office practices, procedures, and equipment. Excellent time management skills. Experience providing administrative or programmatic support. Demonstrated working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook and Internet research. Demonstrated ability to multi-task in a fast-paced and diverse environment. Excellent oral and written communication skills and ability to work independently and in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in an educational setting, including student systems database (such as Banner), electronic purchasing systems (such as eVA). Working knowledge of university and state policies/procedures. Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a cover letter and resume Employment Conditions: Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Classification: Classified Staff Normal Work Schedule: 8am-5pm Employee Classification: Admin & Office Spec III Department: RUC-Health & Human Services Salary: $38,000 - $43,500 (Commensurate with experience and qualifications) Department Contact Name: Glen Mayhew Department Contact Phone: 831-7634 Department Contact Email: gmayhew@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 2e8c284a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Administrative / Clerical Administrative / Clerical Locations Roanoke, Virginia, United States Roanoke, Virginia, United States First Name (required) fb4bc907 Last Name (required) 33bf80b3 Email (required) 33118a9d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the Univer