    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/associate-director-student-involvement-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Involvement",
      "description": "Associate Director, Student Involvement - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Associate Director, Student Involvement Radford, Virginia, United States Administrative & Professional Faculty Student Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Associate Director, Student Involvement Application Review Date: 9/14/2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Reporting to the Director for Student Involvement, the Associate Director is responsible for supporting leadership development through the cultivation and creation of programs, workshops, and engagement opportunities that promote student learning in the areas of leadership and community engagement. This position advises the Radford University Highlander Student Media, made up of The Tartan newspaper, the Beehive yearbook, Radio Free Radford, Radford On Camera (ROC) TV, Whim online magazine, and Exit 109 literary magazine and oversees the administrative aspects of these six student media organizations. The Associate Director also serves as the advisor for the Club Programming Committee and oversee the process of funding $65,000+ dollars to support clubs and organizations. The Associate Director works closely with the Director to coordinate signature departmental programs and initiatives including new student orientation (Quest), Welcome Weeks, Club Fairs, Family Weekend, and holiday and break special programming. This position supervises two assistant directors and provides leadership for the department in the absence of the Director. Required Qualifications A demonstrated ability for collaboration, organization, and bold advancement of new initiatives; a demonstrated ability to work effectively with diverse constituent groups; A strong understanding of the value of the role of student activities within a university environment and the ability to apply student development principles and learning outcomes theories; Demonstrated application of effective assessment strategies, strong communication and marketing skills. Expertise in new student training techniques and leadership development; An advanced degree or a combination of education, training, and experience equivalent to an advanced degree. Professional working experience post-masters; Strong interpersonal and creative problem-solving skills as well as community development competence, a collaborative approach, and a learning mindset are a must. Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience with developing and delivering targeted student programming initiatives. Building relationships and developing program buy-in across both internal and external constituent groups. Experience with and knowledge of supervisory practices and principles; experience in recruiting, hiring, training, and managing employees; Experience in managing multiple budgets and strong organizational skills in handling multiple priorities within established timelines; Demonstrated efficient, effective, and engaging public speaking. Engagement with professional higher education associations (i.e. NASPA, ACUI, NACA, ACPA, AAC&U). 3-5 years post-masters experience in relevant areas of Student Affairs or a combination of education, experience, and training that would produce the required knowledge and abilities could be considered. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Administrative & Professional Faculty Normal Work Schedule: M-F 8:00 -5:00, some evenings and weekends Employee Classification: Professional - Lecturer Department: Student Center Admin Salary: $49,098 - $58,000, Commensurate with experience and qualifications. Department Contact Name: Jen Rentschler Department Contact Phone: 5408317276 Department Contact Email: jrentschler@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 16005885 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Student Affairs Student Affairs Categories Student Affairs / Services Student Affairs / Services Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) c5060b2e Last Name (required) 8c4cfa8c Email (required) 596dcc23 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) fbb311d4 Last Name (required) f16f1100 Email (required) 6963b1ab Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
