    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/assistant-coach-women-s-flag-football-club-part-time-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Flag Football Club (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Assistant Coach, Women's Flag Football Club (Part-Time) - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Coach, Women's Flag Football Club (Part-Time) Radford, Virginia, United States Hourly Wage/Part-Time Student Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Coach, Women's Flag Football Club (Part-Time) Application Review Date: 08/31/2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description The Assistant Coach for the Radford University Women's Flag Football Club Team will support all aspects of the program's operation with a primary emphasis on offensive development, recruiting, and student-athlete success. The Assistant Coach will work closely with the Head Coach to develop and implement offensive strategies, recruit prospective student-athletes, and contribute to the continued growth and competitive success of the Women's Flag Football program within Elevated Club Sports. Required Qualifications • Education, training, and experience in a related field. • Knowledge of football and/or flag football offensive concepts and strategies. • Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. • Ability to recruit and effectively engage prospective student-athletes. • Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required. Preferred Qualifications: • Previous coaching experience at the collegiate, high school, club, or youth level. • Experience recruiting student-athletes. • Experience with film breakdown and game analysis software. • Playing or coaching experience in football or flag football. • CPR, First Aid, and AED certifications (or ability to obtain upon hire). Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: Yes Is this position 100% telework: No Hours Per Week: An average of 29 hours per week Months per Year: TBD Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Classification: H