    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/associate-director-highlander-center-for-character-and-public-impact-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact",
      "description": "Associate Director, Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Associate Director, Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact Radford, Virginia, United States Administrative & Professional Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Associate Director, Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact Application Review Date: 09/04/26 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Make a difference while making a living! The Radford University Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact seeks a motivated individual to manage large projects aimed at building students' capacities to live lives of meaning and purpose through integration of character and public impact into the curriculum and outreach to community partners. This person plans and coordinates large events, coordinates with community partners and other campus offices to achieve Center and University goals, assists with assessment and annual reporting, coordinates our communications platforms (including social media and campus announcements), assists with the budget, supervises student workers, and oversees the physical space of the Center. For a candidate with the right credentials and experience, designing and teaching a course may be an option. This position is grant-funded through June 2028 and may be extended beyond that time frame. More information about the Highlander Center for Character and Public Impact can be found here: https://www.radford.edu/humanities-behavioral-sciences/highlander-center-for-character-public-impact/index.html Required Qualifications •A Master's degree •At least three years of experience in a higher education or non-profit setting •Demonstrated commitment to individual and community flourishing through character development. •Evidence of excellent organizational skills in 