    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/undergraduate-progression-and-graduation-coordinator-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Progression and Graduation Coordinator",
      "description": "Undergraduate Progression and Graduation Coordinator - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Undergraduate Progression and Graduation Coordinator Radford, Virginia, United States Classified Staff Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Undergraduate Progression and Graduation Coordinator Application Review Date: 06/05/2026 (Ongoing - open until filled) Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description The Progression & Graduation Coordinator performs, coordinates, and provides analysis of BSN student progression and graduation activities and provides analyses for both the Radford and Roanoke locations for the College of Nursing under supervision of the Assistant Dean of Undergraduate Nursing. Essential Job Functions • Provides leadership through coordination of all BSN progression and graduation activities in the College Nursing. • Serves as the administrator for the online student management platform and tracks BSN student progression and graduation using this system. • Provides admission, progression, and graduation analyses and reporting to the Assistant Dean of Undergraduate Nursing and executive leadership team for strategic planning and regulatory and accreditation reporting. • Schedules prelicensure BSN students for upper-division coursework. • Supports college budget control and collaborates with relevant parties through assisting with faculty instructional travel and procurement processes to ensure the college maintains compliance with university and Commonwealth policies and procedures. • Designs student progression and graduation documents for distribution to students via email, the college website, and social media which meet university requirements and reflect the professional image of the college. • Provides reports to the Assistant Dean of Undergraduate Nursing, college executive team, and faculty on all progression and graduation initiatives. • Serves as a resource for faculty, staff, and students on progression and graduation matters for the college. • Performs general office administrative assistant duties and other duties as assigned. • Coordination responsibilities include ongoing collaboration with the administrative staff at Radford's main campus and the university's Roanoke sites. Required Qualifications • Strong interpersonal communication skills with frequent contact with students, faculty, and administrators; able to effectively present to groups. • Demonstrated effective and trusted leader who demonstrates successful administrative skills in a fast-paced environment. • Ability to independently perform complex tracking via online student management platform. • Skilled in multifactorial data analysis and report writing. • Demonstrated ability to monitor and bring closure to team activities to meet deadlines. • Ability to work with other administrators, faculty, staff, and students inside and outside the college in a collegial manner. Preferred Qualifications: Education, training and/or experience in healthcare and/or higher education Experience with database management Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a cover letter and resume. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Classification: Classified Staff Employee Classification: Education Support Spec II Department: Undergraduate Nursing Dept. Salary: $38,000 - $43,000 (Commensurate with experience and qualifications) Department Contact Name: Meagan Arthur Department Contact Phone: 540-831-7274 Department Contact Email: marthur4@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 7996ff6f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Administrative / Clerical Academic Affairs Administrative / Clerical Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) a5a98d2b Last Name (required) 8dc065b7 Email (required) 2cd4438b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar 