    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/assistant-director-admissions-roanoke-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Admissions",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Admissions - Roanoke, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Director, Admissions Roanoke, Virginia, United States Classified Staff Enrollment Mgmt & Strategic Comms Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Director, Admissions Application Review Date: August 3, 2026 Campus Location: Roanoke Job Description Radford University is seeking a dynamic and driven Assistant Director of Admissions to join our team at the Radford University Carilion campus in Roanoke, Virginia. This position plays a vital role in advancing the University's enrollment goals by managing a designated recruitment territory, cultivating meaningful relationships with prospective students and families, and serving as a key ambassador for Radford University and its academic programs. The Assistant Director will be responsible for the full scope of territory recruitment — from prospect generation and high school outreach to college fairs, community college visits, and yield initiatives. This individual will develop and implement strategic, territory-specific recruitment plans, including leveraging social media platforms to engage prospective students throughout the recruitment and yield process. Building and nurturing partnerships with area high schools, community-based organizations, and community partners will be central to this role. In addition to regional recruitment responsibilities, this position serves as the primary on-campus contact for daily prospective student visits and group tours at Radford University Carilion, delivering a welcoming, informative, and professional admissions experience in collaboration with the Campus Visit team. The ideal candidate is highly motivated, goal-oriented, and detail-focused, with the ability to multitask, work independently, and thrive as part of a small, collaborative team. Comfort working autonomously is essential. Strong verbal, written, interpersonal, and computer skills are required, along with a genuine passion for working with diverse student populations and families. This position requires the ability to travel both in and out of state in support of recruitment initiatives, as well as the ability to lift or move materials weighing up to 20 pounds. Required Qualifications •Prior work experience in the field of Admissions, Marketing, or related field. •Must be able to conduct extensive local travel for recruitment •Must hold a valid driver’s license and good driving record •Proficient with Microsoft Office suite •Ability to provide direct outreach through excellent written and verbal communication skills •Manage multiple tasks and work independently in a fast-paced environment •Strong organizational skills and ability to focus on details to oversee recruitment territory •Have a high level of energy, enthusiasm, and professionalism Preferred Qualifications: •Demonstrated relevant experience in Admissions, Marketing, or related field •Experience working with a Student Information System (SIS) and a Customer Relations Management (CRM) software •Experience in developing and managing presentations through public speaking with diverse constituencies •Prior experience in admissions, student services, or related higher education settings •Possess a minimum of 2 years’ relevant admissions experience and a willingness to travel •Fluency in Spanish Special Instructions to Applicants This position is located at our Radford University- Carilion campus in Roanoke, Virginia. Employment Conditions: Valid driver's license. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Classified Staff Normal Work Schedule: 40 hours per week, some nights and weekends Employee Classification: Education Support Spec III Department: Admissions Salary: $47,000 - $55,000 (depending on experience) Department Contact Name: Gina Stike Department Contact Phone: 5408315585 Department Contact Email: gstike@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert fae60cf7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Enrollment Management, E&G Enrollment Management, E&G Categories Other Student Affairs / Services Other Student Affairs / Services Locations Roanoke, Virginia, United States Roanoke, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 64a30a71 Last Name (required) e90faa70 Email (required) 383fc8e4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) 6e9971b0 Last Name (required) 9afa2d65 Email (required) 02e375d6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
