    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/director-of-corporate-foundation-relations-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Corporate & Foundation Relations",
      "description": "Director of Corporate & Foundation Relations - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Director of Corporate & Foundation Relations Radford, Virginia, United States Administrative & Professional Faculty University Advancement Add to favorites View favorites Title: Director of Corporate & Foundation Relations Application Review Date: 08/08/26 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description The Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations is responsible for leading a comprehensive program to identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward corporate and foundation partners in support of the University’s strategic priorities. This position plays a critical role in proactively researching funding opportunities, aligning institutional needs with external funders, and developing competitive proposals that advance academic, student success, and institutional initiatives. The Director serves as the University’s primary liaison for corporate and foundation engagement and works collaboratively across campus to build a robust pipeline of institutional funding opportunities. Success in this role will be measured by the development of a strong funding pipeline, the number and quality of proposals submitted, and the growth of corporate and foundation philanthropic support. Required Qualifications • Advanced degree from an accredited institution, or a bachelor’s degree with experience that equates to an advanced degree. • Demonstrated experience in fundraising, development, corporate relations, foundation relations, or grant writing. • Experience developing and submitting grant proposals, letters of inquiry, or similar funding requests. • Proven ability to manage a portfolio of prospects or donors. • Experience conducting prospect research and evaluating funding opportunities. • Ability to build and maintain relationships with external partners and internal stakeholders. • Proficiency with CRM systems or donor databases (e.g., Raiser’s Edge or similar platform) • Ability to represent an organization in professional settings with corporate and foundation partners. • Must have the availability to travel and work non-traditional hours as needed to carry out responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications: • Higher education fundraising experience, particularly in corporate and foundation relations. • Experience working with large, complex, multi-disciplinary grant proposals. • Experience presenting to senior leadership, faculty, or external boards. Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a resume and cover letter. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: Yes FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Administrative & Professional Faculty Employee Classification: Administrative - Lecturer Department: Advancement-MG Salary: $86,000 - $106,000 (Commensurate with experience and qualifications) Department Contact Name: Sharon Ratcliffe Department Contact Phone: 540-831-6716 Department Contact Email: srratcliffe@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 512147c4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments University Advancement University Advancement Categories Advancement Fundraising Advancement Fundraising Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 6ee61340 Last Name (required) 6aec19c9 Email (required) 1e91322c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) c2df6fcc Last Name (required) b9dfddf3 Email (required) cfa0ac6e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equa