    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/communications-and-alumni-coordinator-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Communications and Alumni Coordinator",
      "description": "Communications and Alumni Coordinator - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Communications and Alumni Coordinator Radford, Virginia, United States Classified Staff Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Communications and Alumni Coordinator Application Review Date: 07/31/26 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description The College of Nursing is seeking applicants for a new role in the largest and rapidly growing college at Radford University. The Communications & Alumni Coordinator provides day-to-day communications and digital support for the College of Nursing, executing approved content plans and assisting with routine communication tasks across web, social media, and alumni channels. This position works in close coordination with Alumni Relations as well as the College’s assigned Communications Partner within the central Office of Marketing and Communication, who leads communication strategy, develops messaging plans, and oversees brand alignment. This role is focused on internal and external content execution, administrative coordination, digital asset management, and alumni relations and event planning. The Communications & Alumni Coordinator works with the Dean and the Communications Partner in developing the college communication strategy and focuses on implementing approved plans to serve as a reliable point of coordination between the College of Nursing, centralized communication resources, and Alumni Relations. Essential Job Functions: Faculty, Student, and Alumni Communications Support • Assists with internal content preparation, i.e., faculty, student, and research communications, including newsletters, event promotions, and announcements. • Assists with content preparation for alumni communications, including newsletters, event promotions, and announcements, following templates and plans developed by the Dean in coordination with the Communications Partner. • Coordinates internal logistics and communication details for college and alumni events in partnership with the Dean’s Office and other related university offices. Social Media Execution • Executes the College of Nursing’s social media plan by scheduling and posting pre-approved content across designated platforms. • Assists with basic content organization and tracking to support the College’s and Communications Partner’s social media strategy and editorial calendar. • Monitors engagement activity and reports basic metrics to the Dean and assigned Communications Partner. Website & Digital Content Support • Performs routine content updates to the College of Nursing website within the university’s content management system (CMS), including page edits, uploads, and basic website administration for the college. • Assists with updating website content, faculty and staff listings, announcements, and event content as directed by college leadership and the assigned Communications Partner. • Ensures web content remains accurate, organized, and consistent with university brand and messaging standards. Brand & Messaging Coordination • Helps ensure college communications align with university brand standards and messaging guidelines in collaboration with the assigned Communications Partner. • Serves as a point of coordination between the College of Nursing, the Dean’s Office, Alumni Relations, and central Marketing & Communication for routine communication needs. • Routes communication requests that exceed the scope of this role to the Communications Partner or central Marketing & Communication team via established workflows. Photo & Video Collection • Supports the collection of photo and video content from College of Nursing events not covered by the Communications Partners or central Marketing & Communication resources. • Coordinates with the Communications Partner to ensure collected assets to be posted on digital platforms align with current content plans and institutional storytelling needs. Digital File Management • Ensures content assets are properly labeled, archived, and accessible for use by the College and Communications Partner. Required Qualifications • Experience with digital content management systems (CMS) and social media platforms. • Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines. • Strong written and verbal communication skills. • Ability to work collaboratively with college leadership, the assigned Communications Partner, and Alumni Relations. • Attention to detail and commitment to producing accurate, brand-consistent content. • Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise good professional judgment. • Basic photography / videography skills for event coverage. Education and Experience • Education, experience and/or training in communications, marketing, digital media, English or a related field. • 1 to 3 years of experience in communications support, digital content, social media coordination, or related role. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience with web content management systems (e.g., Modern Campus CMS, WordPress, or similar). • Familiarity with social media scheduling tools and basic analytics platforms. • Experience working in higher education, healthcare, or a comparable professional environment. • Basic photo editing or digital asset management experience. • Familiarity with email marketing tools or newsletter platforms. Education and Experience • Experience in higher education, healthcare communications, or working within a centralized marketing/communications structure. Special Instructions to Applicants Submit resume, cover letter, and samples of social media and/or digital content creation with application. Applicants who are invited for interviews will be asked to bring a portfolio of previous work related to digital and alumni communications. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Classified Staff Normal Work Schedule: Between the hours of 8-5 M-F Employee Classification: Media Specialist III Department: Nursing, College of Salary: $45,739-$49,500 (Commensurate with experience and qualifications) Department Contact Name: Taryn Tretick Department Contact Phone: 540-831-7656 Department Contact Email: ttretick@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1c0d3ae1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Design / Graphic Design / Industrial Design Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Design / Graphic Design / Industrial Design Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 0c786079 Last Name (required) 4ff34b97 Email (required) 6d4d77a7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) 7b0dfe88 Last Name (required) 149c1d2a Email (required) 20bcd93d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the m