    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/executive-director-of-career-and-talent-development-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Career and Talent Development",
      "description": "Executive Director of Career and Talent Development - Radford, Virginia, United States Home About Radford University Benefits and Wellness Applicant Login Candidate Settings Kiosk mode Executive Director of Career and Talent Development Radford, Virginia, United States Administrative & Professional Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Executive Director of Career and Talent Development Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Radford University seeks a collaborative and energetic leader to serve as the Executive Director of the Center for Career and Talent Development. Reporting to the Associate Provost for Academic Affairs, the Director provides strategic leadership and direction for a team responsible for developing, implementing, and evaluating career and talent development opportunities, programs, and events that connect employer partners with the university's students, faculty, and alumni. The portfolio of the Executive Director for The Center for Career and Talent Development includes strategic vision, employer cultivation and engagement, career exploration, talent development, job placement, student employment support, personal and professional development, and the development of a Student Employment unit within the Center. The Director cultivates and secures key external relationships, partnerships and opportunities; serves as an expert on industry trends and needs and how they can help inform students on current talent acquisition processes and inform areas of opportunities for Radford and what we offer for students; develops collaborations with advising, faculty, colleges and other internal leaders across academic affairs, economic development, advancement and alumni relations; and creates and assesses programs. Externally, the Director will serve on professional boards, such as VACE (Virginia Association for Colleges and Employers), the SCHEV work-based learning initiatives, or NACE or career center director consortium. This oversight will include leadership and development of the professional and student staff in the department and budget management. Required Qualifications Track record of success and experience in leading change and employer cultivation and engagement. Experience in planning and assessing career development, professional development, human resources management, or corporate talent acquisition programs and strategies. Management experience in and knowledge of the employment needs of corporate, non-profit, governmental, educational, or entrepreneurial ventures and organizations. Proven ability in building relationships and strategic partnerships with a wide range of internal and external constituents. Appreciation for the role of higher education in preparing students for future career success. Evidence of a varied career with progressively responsible supervisory and management experience; demonstrated experience in developing strategy and or strategic vision, budget leadership and management. Excellent communication skills and professionalism with proven ability to navigate across diverse internal and external stakeholders. Strong fiscal planning and budget management abilities. Proficient with current office software with the ability utilize current technology and social media. Experience working with diverse populations. Education: Advanced degree; or a Bachelors degree with experience that equates to an advanced degree. Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree and significant experience in career services, talent acquisition related fields or equivalent training, education, or experience. Talent management and leading strategic plans. Special Instructions to Applicants Spelman Johnson is assisting with the search for candidates. Applications can be submitted at this link: https://spelmanandjohnson.com/position/executive-director-of-career-and-talent-development/ Applications are not being accepted on this website. Please use the link provided above to apply. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: 40 Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: Yes FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Administrative & Professional Faculty Employee Classification: Administrative - Lecturer Department: Career Services Salary: $90,000 - $130,000 (Commensurate with experience and qualifications) Department Contact Name: Jeanne Mekolichick Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5114 Department Contact Email: jmekolic@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d2434102 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments AA-Local Auxiliary AA-Local Auxiliary Categories Academic Affairs Executive / Director / Management Student Affairs / Services Academic Affairs Executive / Director / Management Student Affairs / Services Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 223ba564 Last Name (required) f97d22ba Email (required) 8056e444 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Admissions Counselor Enrollment Management, E&G The Admissions Counselor works directly with Deans, faculty, and staff, as needed, in the development of an effective, data-informed enrollment planning process to recruit a pool of students meeting the University’s strategic goals for all populations of students. The Admissions Counselor is responsible for meeting the enrollment goals of the University by independently developing and managing a specific assigned recruitment territory to identify, attract, select and enroll diverse and qualified students to Radford University. Through oversight of prospect generation, recruitment travel, outreach, and yield efforts related to both students and families, this position will establish direct territory-specific initiatives to meet territory recruitment goals.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will be expected to engage in extensive recruitment travel (including evening, weekend, and extended overnight); conducting recruitment presentations across a territory; serving as ambassadors for Radford University to visiting prospective students and families; as well as advising potential freshman and transfer students on admissions procedures, policies, and pathways. The Admissions Counselor will develop an in-depth understanding of admissions practices, institutional policies, and program offerings to effectively recruit students.\n\nThe Admissions Counselor will also implement a domestic student recruitment plan which includes high school visits, two-year college visits, college fairs, information sessions, receptions, and meetings with secondary school and independent counselors, prospective students, families, and community-based organizations, and support the recruitment and admission of transfer students from institutions within the assigned territory. Project & Event Manager Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a Project & Event Manager to oversee the day-to-day direction and coordination of Facilities maintenance projects and campus event support. This position manages scheduling, vendor communication, procurement, cost tracking, and customer estimates for renovation projects and events. Equipment Repair Technician Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking an Equipment Repair Technician to provide maintenance and repair services for motor vehicles and grounds care equipment on the Main Campus in Radford, VA. Apply Now First Name (required) 22901642 Last Name (required) 19370f44 Email (required) 9b22a8bb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Quick Links About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Radford University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
